test:
In tests/record-store/SP-text-scan.test.ts, next to SP-08, using its helpers and `bucketIndex`:

it.each(['memory','sqlite'] as const)('SP-08c %s: a prefix that becomes composite leaves the loaded old prefix', async (kind) => {
  const backend = await store(kind, { schemas: withTextIndex(bucketIndex) });
  try {
    await seed(backend, [widget('p1','n1',{ bucket:'A', topic:'shared' })], 'sp08c');
    expect(refs(await search(backend,{ index:'sp-bucket', values:['A'], terms:['shared'], limit:20 }))).toEqual([keyOf('p1','n1')]);
    await seed(backend, [widget('p1','n1',{ bucket:{}, topic:'shared' }, 2)], 'sp08d', 1);
    expect(refs(await search(backend,{ index:'sp-bucket', values:['A'], terms:['shared'], limit:20 }))).toEqual([]);
  } finally { await backend.close(); }
});

Plus a SQLite two-connection variant in the style of SP-09:
1. `first` opens with withTextIndex(bucketIndex), seeds n1 with bucket 'A', and searches ['A'] (gets [n1]).
2. `second = open('sqlite', { path: first.path!, schemas: withTextIndex(bucketIndex) })` commits n1 rev 2 with bucket {} (expectedRevision 1), then closes.
3. `first` searches ['A'] again and expects [].

Before the fix, the sqlite case of SP-08c and the two-connection variant both return [keyOf('p1','n1')] and fail. The memory case already passes. After either fix, all of them pass.
